{"name":"Rambutan","hex":"#a94737","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rambutan","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree of species Nephelium lappaceum, of Southeast Asia.","The edible fruit of this tree. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rambutan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rambutan","blocks":[{"text":"Rambutan is a medium-sized tropical tree in the family Sapindaceae, and the edible fruit of this tree. The fruit is sweet, with a hairy leathery rind and a single seed. The rambutan is native to Southeast Asia; its centre of diversity is in Indonesia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Rambutan_white_background_alt.jpg/330px-Rambutan_white_background_alt.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rambutan"},{"title":"Rambutan (cryptography)","blocks":[{"text":"Rambutan is a family of encryption technologies designed by the Communications-Electronics Security Group (CESG), the technical division of the United Kingdom government's secret communications agency, GCHQ."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rambutan_(cryptography)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Rambutans_by_Muhammad_Mahdi_Karim.jpg/500px-Rambutans_by_Muhammad_Mahdi_Karim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Rambutans_by_Muhammad_Mahdi_Karim.jpg/500px-Rambutans_by_Muhammad_Mahdi_Karim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARambutans_by_Muhammad_Mahdi_Karim.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Nephelium_lappaceum_at_Kota_Damansara_20240101_133139.jpg/250px-Nephelium_lappaceum_at_Kota_Damansara_20240101_133139.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or